# Claude Code — ignore local settings but track shared skills
.claude

# brokkr local cache, with one deliberate exception.
#
# gate.db holds the sync-bench baseline rows that brokkr.toml pins by UUID.
# It was the ONLY copy of those numbers: the pin is committed, the row it
# points at was not, so anything that removed the file orphaned every
# baseline on the host with no recovery path. That is not hypothetical -
# `brokkr clean` deleted this directory wholesale (fixed upstream in
# 9e0d0ce), and `brokkr kill`'s graceful path calls it, so one SIGTERM'd
# bench wiped every baseline at once. Losing a baseline is worse than it
# sounds: gates like `meta.provider_requests` are `max_delta = 0`, and
# re-recording silently rebases them onto current numbers, so a regression
# gets blessed as the new reference and the gate goes blind.
#
# Tracking it costs a binary diff whenever a baseline is recorded, which is
# rare and deliberate. That is the cheaper side of the trade.
#
# The three-step form is required: git will not re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so the directories must stay walkable.
.brokkr/*
!.brokkr/ratatoskr/
.brokkr/ratatoskr/*
!.brokkr/ratatoskr/gate.db

